[0,"o","Recorded replay: completed average bug repair with Claude Code + Kimi Coding.\r\n"]
[0.002,"o","All tests pass.\r\n\r\n**The bug:** `average` in `src/task.mjs` returned the raw sum from `reduce` without dividing by the array length, so `average([2,4])` returned `6` instead of `3`.\r\n\r\n**Fix** (one line, tests untouched):\r\n```js\r\nexport const average=xs=>xs.length?xs.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/xs.length:0;\r\n```\r\n- Divide the sum by `xs.length` to compute the mean.\r\n- Return `0` for an empty array (avoids `NaN` from `0/0`).\r\n\r\n**Test results** (`node --test tests.mjs`):\r\n- Before fix: 1 pass, 1 fail (`case 0`: got 6, expected 3)\r\n- After fix: 2 pass, 0 fail\r\n"]
[0.003,"o","$ node --test tests.mjs\r\n"]
